                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "tag": "past_simple",
                    "title": "Past simple: negatives and questions",
                    "explanation": "En negativa usamos «didn't» + verbo en forma base (nunca «I didn't went»):\n- «I didn't go to university.»\n\nEn preguntas: «Did» + sujeto + verbo en forma base. Con palabras interrogativas, igual:\n- «Did you live near the sea? — Yes, I did. / No, I didn't.»\n- «Why did you leave Spain?»\n\nRecuerda los irregulares de esta unidad: «grow» → «grew», «give» → «gave», «leave» → «left», «go» → «went».\n\nExpresiones útiles: «when I was six», «three years ago», «last summer», «in 2015».",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "",
                        "Ejemplo"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "Afirmativa",
                          "I studied design. My dad gave me a guitar."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Negativa",
                          "I didn't go to university."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Pregunta",
                          "Did you live near the sea?"
                        ],
                        [
                          "Respuesta corta",
                          "Yes, I did. / No, I didn't."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Pregunta con Wh-",
                          "Why did you leave Spain?"
                        ],
                        [
                          "Cuándo",
                          "when I was six, ten years ago, last summer"
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "We went to the beach every summer.",
                      "I didn't see the sea very often.",
                      "Did you play music when you were a child?",
                      "Why did you leave Spain?"
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "tag": "used_to",
                    "title": "used to: past habits",
                    "explanation": "«Used to» + verbo describe hábitos o situaciones del pasado que ya no son así. Es igual para todas las personas:\n- «We used to go to the beach every summer.» (íbamos a la playa todos los veranos; ahora no)\n- «I / she / they used to live in Valencia.»\n\nLa negativa es «didn't use to» (sin d) y la pregunta, «Did you use to…?»:\n- «I didn't use to like coffee.»\n- «Did you use to play the guitar?»\n\nPara algo que pasó una sola vez se usa el past simple, no «used to»:\n- «My dad gave me a guitar when I was eight.»",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "",
                        "Ejemplo"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "Afirmativa",
                          "We used to go to the beach every summer."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Negativa",
                          "I didn't use to practise much."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Pregunta",
                          "Did you use to live near the sea?"
                        ],
                        [
                          "Una sola vez → past simple",
                          "My dad gave me a guitar when I was eight."
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "We used to go to the beach every summer.",
                      "Sam used to work in a pub.",
                      "I didn't use to like tea, but now I drink it every day.",
                      "Did you use to play music when you were a child?"
                    ]
                  }
                },
